fieldsmith 1
# === FIELDSMITH LITERATE CASE ===
# @id: A5
# @code: A5
# @category: analytic
# @level: Analytic Verification
# @title: Analytic Benchmark A5: Cylindrical Regenerative Cooling — Hot-Gas Heat Flux + Coolant Convection Thermo-Elastic Lamé (V60c)
# @subtitle: Verify coupled steady conduction and thermo-elastic stress on a CuCrZr chamber wall with inward hot-gas Neumann heatflux (q = 5.0) on the bore and outward Robin convection (h = 0.25, T_inf = 20 °C) on the coolant jacket.
# @verification_badge: Verified by V60(c) · Exact Robin–Neumann Logarithmic Thermo-Elasticity · PASS (< 2.0%)
# @doc_path: docs/analytic-tests/A5-regenerative-cooling-robin-lame.md
# @fsm_path: examples/analytic/A5-regenerative-cooling-robin-lame.fsm
# @starter_fsm_name: a5-regenerative-cooling-robin-lame.fsm
# @verification_refs: docs/verification/V20.md, docs/verification/V60.md
# ---
# @check: Robin–Neumann Logarithmic Temperature T(r) at r = 11 / 15 / 19 mm || T(r) = T_∞ + r_i q_in [1/(r_o h_c) + ln(r_o / r)] = 30.0 + 50.0 ln(20 / r) || 59.892 / 44.384 / 32.565 °C || 59.694 / 44.224 / 32.464 °C || 0.33% / 0.36% / 0.31% || ≤ 2.0%
# @check: Thermo-Elastic Radial Expansion u_r(r) at r = 11 / 15 / 19 mm || u_r(r) = C₁ r + (C₂ + γ α ∫ s ΔT(s) ds) / r || 6.493 / 9.410 / 10.580 µm || 6.402 / 9.290 / 10.430 µm || 1.41% / 1.28% / 1.42% || ≤ 2.5%
# @check: Thermo-Elastic Axial Stress σ_zz(r) & In-Plane Sum σ_rr + σ_θθ || σ_zz(r) = 2λ C₁ − 2μ γ α ΔT(r)  (at r = 11 / 15 / 19 mm) || -105.24 / -54.11 / -15.14 MPa || -103.73 / -52.21 / -12.71 MPa || 1.24% / 1.57% / 2.01% (of bore scale) || ≤ 3.0%
# ---
# @assert: Robin–Neumann Bore Peak Temperature T(r_i) || max_temp || 64.657 || 2.5% || °C
# @assert: Robin–Neumann Jacket Outer Temperature T(r_o) || min_temp || 30.000 || 6.0% || °C
# @assert: Thermo-Elastic Bore Peak von Mises Stress || max_vm_elem || 118.0 || 6.0% || MPa
# ---
# @step: 1. Coupled Neumann Hot-Gas Heat Flux + Robin Coolant Convection Boundary Conditions || setup
#   Open Setup (2). In a regeneratively cooled rocket chamber, the wall temperatures are not known a priori: instead, hot combustion gas injects a surface heat flux q_in = 5.0 into the inner bore (r_i = 10 mm) while liquid coolant flowing through the outer jacket (r_o = 20 mm) extracts heat by forced convection q_out = h_c (T(r_o) − T_∞) with h_c = 0.25 and T_∞ = 20.0 °C.
# @expected:
#   Setup shows Heat Flux hot_gas_flux (q = 5.0) on skin_in and Convection coolant_conv (h = 0.25, tinf = 20 °C) on skin_out.
# @step: 2. Verify the Exact Logarithmic Temperature Profile T(r) = 30 + 50 ln(20/r) in Results (3) || results
#   Switch to Results (3) and select "Temperature". Radial conservation of energy 2π r_i q_in = 2π r_o h_c (T(r_o) − T_∞) pins the outer jacket wall at exactly T(r_o) = 20 + (10 × 5.0)/(20 × 0.25) = 30.0 °C, rising logarithmically through the wall to T(r_i) = 30 + 50 ln(2) = 64.657 °C at the hot-gas bore. Then switch to "Stress" to inspect the compressive bore stress (σ_zz = −121 MPa, σ_θθ = −70 MPa at r_i) balanced by outer jacket hoop tension (+49.6 MPa at r_o).
# @expected:
#   Temperature ranges from 30.0 °C on the outer wall to 64.7 °C on the inner bore, matching the exact Robin–Neumann formula to 0.35%.
# ---
# @theory_title: Analytic Verification A5 — Cylindrical Robin–Neumann Conduction & Duhamel–Neumann Thermo-Elasticity (V60c)
# @theory_summary:
#   Derives the exact 1D cylindrical temperature distribution under mixed Neumann–Robin boundary conditions and integrates the resulting logarithmic thermal strain field in closed form.
# @theory_section: A5.1 Mixed Neumann–Robin Cylindrical Conduction & Exact Thermal Moment Integral f(r)
# @theory_eq:
#   −(1/r) d/dr(r dT/dr) = 0,   −dT/dr|_{r_i} = q_in,   −dT/dr|_{r_o} = h_c(T(r_o) − T_∞)
#   T(r) = T_∞ + (r_i q_in)/(r_o h_c) + r_i q_in ln(r_o / r)
#   f(r) = ∫_{r_i}^r s ΔT(s) ds = ½ ΔT_in (r² − r_i²) − r_i q_in [½ r² ln(r/r_i) − ¼(r² − r_i²)]
# @theory_body:
#   Substituting f(r) into the Duhamel–Neumann radial equilibrium equation yields the exact radial displacement u_r(r) = C₁ r + (C₂ + γα f(r))/r and thermal stress components σ_rr(r), σ_θθ(r), σ_zz(r) with zero free-parameter fitting.
# ---
# @mcp: Solve Regenerative Cooling Thermo-Elastic Benchmark via API || solve || {"kind":"solve","dofs":35000}
#   Run the coupled P2 conduction + thermo-elastic solver on A5.
# === END LITERATE HEADER ===

name "A5 — Regenerative Cooling Robin-Neumann Thermo-Elastic Lame (V60c)"
custommaterial cucrzr_regen name="CuCrZr (E=128 GPa, nu=0.34, a=1.7e-5)" e=128000 nu=0.34 a=1.7e-5 yield=380 density=8.9
material cucrzr_regen

cylinder outer r=20 h=60 at=(0, 0, 30)
cylinder bore r=10 h=60 at=(0, 0, 30) subtract
box cutx size=(90, 45, 160) at=(-45, 0, 0) subtract
box cuty size=(45, 90, 160) at=(0, -45, 0) subtract

region skin_in = bore.side
region skin_out = outer.side
region xplane = cutx.px
region yplane = cuty.py
region zbot = outer.bottom
region ztop = outer.top

support kx xplane fixed=x
support ky yplane fixed=y
support kz_bot zbot fixed=z
support kz_top ztop fixed=z
heatflux hot_gas_flux skin_in q=5.0 case="RegenHotFire"
convection coolant_conv skin_out h=0.25 tinf=20.0 case="RegenHotFire"
solve tref=20.0
